# Schedule

## Summary

Scheduling the runs of an automation with the event Scheduled communications. From the automation list staff open its schedule, add a date and time it should run at, and see its pending times and cancel one. The backend runs the automation when a pending time comes.

## Requirements

- **SCHEDOPEN** — Schedule on an automation with the event Scheduled communications opens "Schedule communication": a date and a time, set to the present moment, with Schedule beneath them, and beside them the automation's pending times. It closes only with its close button.
- **SCHEDADD** — Schedule adds the date and time, in the staff member's local time, to the automation's pending times; an automation switched off is refused. No notice shows either way. The dialog reads the automation again at once, so a time added may show only when the dialog is opened again.
- **PENDING** — The pending times are listed, all at once, with their time and the status "Pending", each with a button that cancels it without asking; the list is read again after. An automation not scheduled before the dialog opened lists none.
- **SCHEDRUN** — The backend looks at the pending times every 20 seconds and runs the automation of each one less than 20 seconds away and in the same minute, without a staff member. The time is then started, with its run, and leaves the pending times. A time missed while the backend was not running stays pending and never runs.
- **STARTED** — Below the pending times, a second list shows the runs of the automation's scheduled times, newest first, 10 to a page: each with the time it started, its progress, whether it is done and whether it failed.

## Tests

- Scheduling an automation that was switched off adds no pending time.
- A time scheduled two minutes ahead runs the automation within those two minutes and 20 seconds, and leaves the pending list.
- Cancelling a pending time removes it from the list, and the automation does not run at that time.
- After a scheduled run, the list of started times shows it with its progress.
- A staff member without `communication:role` cannot schedule an automation on the backend.

## View: ScheduleDialog

### Summary

The dialog that schedules an automation's runs and shows its pending and started times.

### Display

- The date and time pickers, set to the present moment, with Schedule; the dialog closes only with its close button — [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications.schedule#Requirements[SCHEDOPEN])
- The pending times, each with its time, "Pending" and a cancel button — [reads](aim:juicebar.communications#Record:Communication), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications.schedule#Requirements[PENDING])
- The started times, each with its time, progress, done and failed, newest first, page by page — [reads](aim:juicebar.communications#Record:TaskQueue), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications.schedule#Requirements[STARTED])

### Actions

- Schedule — [exposes](aim:juicebar.communications.schedule#Operation:ScheduleCommunication)
- Cancel a pending time — [exposes](aim:juicebar.communications.schedule#Operation:CancelScheduledTime)

### Layout

- The date and time take the left third, the pending and started times the rest.

### Bindings

- binds: `projects/juicebar/src/lib/core/modules/communications/schedule/schedule-dialog/schedule-dialog.component.ts#ScheduleDialogComponent` — as: component
- binds: `projects/juicebar/src/lib/core/modules/communications/schedule/pending-times/pending-times.component.ts#PendingTimesComponent` — as: component
- binds: `projects/juicebar/src/lib/core/modules/communications/schedule/started-times/started-times.component.ts#StartedTimesComponent` — as: component
- binds: `service:communication-service#getCommunication` — as: handler
- binds: `service:communication-service#fetchScheduleForCommunication` — as: handler
- binds: `service:communication-service#getCommunicationQueues` — as: handler
- provenance: inferred

## Operation: ScheduleCommunication

### Summary

A staff member schedules an automation to run at a date and time.

### Input

```schema
communicationId: string required ref(juicebar.communications#Communication.id)
time: datetime required
```

### Authz

- `juicebar.communications#Persona:CommunicationStaff`
- `juicebar.communications#Persona:CommunicationSuperAdmin`

### Ensures

- An active automation gets the time as a pending time, and an inactive one is refused — [mutates](aim:juicebar.communications#Record:Communication), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications.schedule#Requirements[SCHEDADD])
- When the time comes, the backend runs the automation without a staff member and marks the time started with its run — [invokes](aim:juicebar.communications#Operation:RunCommunication), [mutates](aim:juicebar.communications#Record:Communication), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications.schedule#Requirements[SCHEDRUN]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications#Requirements[RUN])
- The operation is refused without `communication:role`; another organisation's automation is scheduled all the same — [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications#Requirements[COMMROLE]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar#Requirements[ROLES]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications#Requirements[COMMORG])

### Bindings

- binds: `projects/juicebar/src/lib/core/modules/communications/schedule/schedule-dialog/schedule-dialog.component.ts#ScheduleDialogComponent.schedule` — as: component
- binds: `service:communication-service#scheduleCommunication` — as: handler
- binds: `juice-modules:packages/juice/src/modules/communications/modules/Communications.ts#Communications.scheduleInterval` — as: handler
- provenance: inferred

## Operation: CancelScheduledTime

### Summary

A staff member cancels a pending time of an automation.

### Input

```schema
communicationId: string required ref(juicebar.communications#Communication.id)
ref: string required
```

### Authz

- `juicebar.communications#Persona:CommunicationStaff`
- `juicebar.communications#Persona:CommunicationSuperAdmin`

### Ensures

- The time leaves the pending times and does not run — [mutates](aim:juicebar.communications#Record:Communication), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications.schedule#Requirements[PENDING])
- The operation is refused without `communication:role`; another organisation's automation is changed all the same — [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications#Requirements[COMMROLE]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar#Requirements[ROLES]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications#Requirements[COMMORG])

### Bindings

- binds: `projects/juicebar/src/lib/core/modules/communications/schedule/pending-times/pending-times.component.ts#PendingTimesComponent.cancel` — as: component
- binds: `service:communication-service#removeFromSchedule` — as: handler
- provenance: inferred
